# CODEOWNERS — automatic review assignment + enforced review.
#
# Each line maps a path pattern to one or more owners (GitHub usernames or
# teams). The LAST matching pattern wins. Owners listed here are automatically
# requested for review on PRs touching those paths. Pair this with a branch
# protection rule on `main` that enables "Require review from Code Owners" so
# these approvals are mandatory to merge.
#
# NOTE: `@qalam/maintainers` is a placeholder team. Create the GitHub teams
# under the `qalam` org (or replace with real @usernames) before enabling the
# branch-protection rule, or PRs will be blocked awaiting a non-existent owner.

# Default owner for everything not matched by a more specific rule below.
*                       @qalam/maintainers

# ── Application code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/backend/               @qalam/maintainers
/frontend/              @qalam/maintainers
/admin/                 @qalam/maintainers
/packages/              @qalam/maintainers

# ── Platform / delivery surfaces (higher blast radius — keep tightly owned) ──
/infrastructure/        @qalam/maintainers
/scripts/               @qalam/maintainers
/.github/               @qalam/maintainers

# CI/CD, release, and rollback pipelines: changes here can ship or break prod.
/.github/workflows/     @qalam/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @qalam/maintainers

# Database migrations — schema changes deserve explicit sign-off.
/backend/src/database/migrations/   @qalam/maintainers

# Documentation.
/docs/                  @qalam/maintainers
